{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["And the sense of <b>at the head and not at the tail</b> is as an explanation: at the head of all the peoples and not at the tail of any one of all the nations, for it is possible that one could be at the head over many peoples and at the tail of one nation more esteemed than oneself. But the correct interpretation is that He will set you at the head from now onward and not at the tail ever, at any time whatsoever; and similarly, only upward always, and you will never be below."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:08.989809898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}